  "stem": "The graphs of \\(y = x^{2} + 4\\) and \\(y = 4x\\) in the \\(xy\\)-plane intersect at exactly one point. What is the \\(y\\)-coordinate of that point?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "8"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "At an intersection, \\(x^{2} + 4 = 4x\\), so \\(x^{2} - 4x + 4 = 0\\).",
    "This is \\((x - 2)^{2} = 0\\), so \\(x = 2\\), and \\(y = 4(2) = 8\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x, y = symbols('x y')\nsols = solve([Eq(y, x**2 + 4), Eq(y, 4*x)], [x, y], dict=True)\nassert len(sols) == 1 and sols[0][y] == 8\nassert Rational(spr_answers[0]) == 8",
